## Context

Daniel approved the weeks 2 to 8 English text on 2026-11-01 ("3. Covers: Approved", owner
answer relayed by the PM session). Five committed tests pinned the shipped draft state, so the
approved data of `jr-green-c85ef735-week-approval.patch` would fail them. This Red aligned the
tests with the owner decision and pinned the approved record.

## Edits (tests only; no production source, no content change)

1. `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-covers-16books-adversarial.test.ts`
   - New helper `copyLevel2WeeksDraftAfterFirst()`: copies the shipped Level 2 weeks to a
     temporary folder (rule 11.1) and forces `approval.text` of weeks 2 to 8 to `{status:'draft'}`.
   - Both ADV-D12 tests (tests 1 and 2) read the copy, not the shipped approval state.
2. `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-covers-16books.test.ts`
   - New helper `draftWeeksEnv()`: a temporary repository root with the drafted week copies, a
     media symbolic link, and a logo symbolic link. The script reads it through `WORKBOOKS_ROOT`;
     `MASTERY_PHONICS_GRAPH` keeps the shipped phonics graph.
   - R22 (test 3) and R22 M21/M22 (test 4) run the script with that environment.
   - New R30: the shipped weeks 2 to 8 must record status approved, date 2026-11-01, words
     "3. Covers: Approved", and a source that names the PM relay.
3. `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-contract-v2.test.ts`
   - Test 5, renamed "keeps the other parts draft in all eight weeks and records the owner
     approval of the weeks 2 to 8 text", requires the approved text record for weeks 2 to 8.
     The other parts stay draft.

