## Mutants (never committed; each restore verified with git diff --quiet)

- MA (caught): `lib/storytime/print/covers.ts`, `storytimeCoverPanelValues` ignored `ctx.weeks`
  and read every shipped week, so the approved-only filtering of D12 was gone. Run: adversarial
  `-t "ADV-D12"`. Both ADV-D12 tests failed (14 > 14 books assertion; 0 > 0 missing-field
  assertion). Restored clean. Evidence: mid-red-c85ef735-mutants.txt.
- MC (caught): `scripts/storytime/make-storytime-book-cover.ts`, `panelReport` recorded every
  week as 'approved', so the build report never named a draft week (the D12 report rule removed).
  Run: 16books `-t "R22: mock reports"`. The test failed on the `/draft/i` report assertion.
  Restored clean (`git diff --quiet`). Evidence: mid-red-c85ef735-mutants.txt.
- MB (caught): the same script, the D12 print stop never fired (`missing.length > 99`). Run:
  16books `-t "R22"` (both R22 tests). Both failed. Detail: the mutant print run passed the D12
  stop, wrote the mock deliverables into the print output folder, and its PDF/X child step then
  failed with `spawnSync … ENOENT` (the child finds no node in this environment), so the exit
  status was 1 for that reason. The tests caught the mutant on the D12 error-message
  assertions: the output held no D12 rejection, and the "no deliverable" state was broken.
  Restored clean (`git diff --quiet`). Evidence: mid-red-c85ef735-mutants.txt.

